:: Himari - Your Name [bg-sanctuary]
<h1 class="ptitle">BELOW DECK</h1>
<<run setup.himari.mark('name')>>
<<addmins 30>>
<br />
You came down to the third deck with her water can at the usual hour and found her cabin door open and the cabin empty. The chain lay coiled on the floor with the cuffs open at the end of it.
<br /><br />
Then you heard them coming back along the corridor: a guard's boots, and the scrape of bare feet beside them. He had her by the arm, still in the thin blue gown from the infirmary. It was the doc's day. She was walking the way she always walked back from the doc, which was the way people walk out of cold water.
<br /><br />
They had to pass you in the narrow corridor. As they did, she lifted her head.
<br /><br />
<center>
	<<image 'people/himari/your_name.jpg'>>
</center>
<br />
<<himari>>
	<<= $player.name>>.
<</himari>>
<br />
She said it quietly and clearly, the whole name, exactly right, the way she must have practised it alone in the dark with no one to hear. It was the first time she had ever said it.
<br /><br />
The guard shoved her forward without breaking step and took her into the cabin, and you heard the cuffs close around her ankles again.
<br /><br />
Up at the top of the stairs, a shape had stopped to watch. Negan, with his bat over his shoulder, leaning on the rail, smiling down at all of you. He had heard it.
<br /><br />
<<negan>>
	Not long now, Dolly.
<</negan>>
<br />
He said it to her, through the open door. Then he looked at you, and he winked, and he went back up the stairs whistling.
<br /><br />
You put the water can down inside her door. When you straightened up she was sitting on the bed with her knees pulled up, the way she had sat on the first day in the container, and she was looking at you, and she did not look away.
<br /><br />
<<link 'Leave'>>
	<<goto 'Sanctuary'>>
<</link>>
